sink|go-below-surface|VERB|go below a liquid surface|To move down into a liquid or below its surface.|chìm|The small stone sank to the bottom of the clear pond.|Viên đá nhỏ chìm xuống đáy ao trong vắt.|Intransitive here; sink, sank, sunk. Transitive sink a ship also occurs.|0
wall|vertical-structure|NOUN|vertical dividing structure|A tall upright structure that encloses, divides, or supports a space.|tường; bức tường|We hung the new map on the wall beside the classroom door.|Chúng tôi treo bản đồ mới lên tường bên cạnh cửa lớp.|Countable; on a wall for an attached object, against a wall for something leaning on it.|0
aspect|part-to-consider|NOUN|one part of a subject|One part or feature of something that can be considered separately.|khía cạnh|The report examines the financial aspect of opening a village library.|Báo cáo xem xét khía cạnh tài chính của việc mở thư viện làng.|Countable: an aspect of something. Use different aspects for multiple features.|0
glad|pleased|ADJECTIVE|feeling pleased|Feeling happy or pleased about something.|vui; hài lòng|I was glad to hear that the missing dog had returned home.|Tôi vui khi biết con chó bị lạc đã trở về nhà.|Usually predicative: glad to do, glad that, glad about something. Not normally a glad person in ordinary description.|0
key|lock-tool|NOUN|tool for a lock|A shaped object used to lock or unlock something.|chìa khóa|Hoa kept the spare key in a sealed envelope at her sister's home.|Hoa cất chìa khóa dự phòng trong một phong bì dán kín ở nhà chị gái.|Countable; a key to a door, unlock a door with a key.|0
key|essential|ADJECTIVE|very important|Important because something depends on it for success or understanding.|chủ chốt; rất quan trọng|Clear signs were a key part of the station's safety plan.|Biển chỉ dẫn rõ ràng là một phần quan trọng trong kế hoạch an toàn của nhà ga.|Often before a noun: a key factor. Also be key to something.|1
key|enter-data|VERB|enter using a keyboard|To enter information by pressing keys on a keyboard.|gõ; nhập dữ liệu bằng bàn phím|The clerk keyed the delivery address into the booking system.|Nhân viên nhập địa chỉ giao hàng vào hệ thống đặt dịch vụ.|Transitive; key information into a system, key in a number. Keyed is the past form.|2
key|keyboard-button|NOUN|button on a keyboard|One of the buttons pressed to type or operate a keyboard.|phím|Press the space key once between the two words.|Nhấn phím cách một lần giữa hai từ.|Countable; press a key. A keyboard has keys; a screen control is normally a button.|3
key|means-to-success|NOUN|important means of achieving something|Something that makes success or understanding possible.|bí quyết; mấu chốt|Regular practice was the key to her confident performance.|Luyện tập đều đặn là bí quyết giúp cô biểu diễn tự tin.|The key to a result; to is a preposition, so the key to improving uses an -ing form.|4
